    "879-3000",
    "879-3001",
    "879-3020",
    "879-3021",
    "879-3040"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "wago.com",
  "description": "Three-phase MID energy meter (4PU, 4PS and 2PU CT variants) with Modbus",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-10-18",
  "source": "Register map as used by the Varitras ha-wago integration, which cites the WAGO energy meter manual 4PU/4PS/2PU CT (EN V1.6), appendix A3.2; not checked against the manual itself",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Varitras/ha-wago, wago_879_api/registers.py (MIT licence)",
      "url": "https://github.com/Varitras/ha-wago/blob/main/custom_components/wago_879/wago_879_api/registers.py",
      "note": "Cites WAGO manual 4PU/4PS/2PU CT, EN V1.6, appendix A3.2"
    },
    {
      "title": "WAGO Energy Meters (MID) product manual",
      "url": "https://www.wago.com/879-3000",
      "note": "The register table is in the manual linked from the product page; it was not reachable when this map was written"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The register addresses come from a third-party Home Assistant integration that quotes the WAGO manual, so the map is unofficial until someone checks it against the manual or a device.",
    "Every measured value is a 32-bit IEEE float in two holding registers, read with function 03, big-endian with the high word first (WAGO's 'Float ABCD'). The exceptions are the whole numbers (meter code, id, quadrants, tariff) and the serial number.",
    "Power is in kW, kvar and kVA and energy in kWh and kvarh, as the integration reports them; check this against the manual, which may list W and Wh.",
    "The 'total' energy registers follow the meter's combination code (0x400F): 1 import only, 2 export only, 3 import plus export, 4 and 5 import minus export. They can fall or go negative; use the import and export registers for rising counters.",
    "Voltage average, current average and the CT ratio sit on registers the manual shades grey: a direct-measuring meter leaves them at zero. A tariff-less meter holds zero in most T1 to T4 and Q1 to Q4 counters.",
    "The meter has its own Modbus RTU interface; the Modbus TCP access in the integration goes through the 879-9000 module, which forwards the meter's unit id (factory setting 1) and answers itself on unit 255. The serial settings are not given in the sources used, so the format's defaults apply.",
    "Writable settings (unit id, CT ratio and others) are in the manual; this map lists the values only."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp+rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "data_bits": 8,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "unofficial",
  "enums": {
    "combination": {"1": "Import only", "2": "Export only", "3": "Import plus export", "4": "Import minus export", "5": "Import minus export"}
  },
